<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saka Haumavarga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Amyrgian Scythians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saka Haumavarga were a Saka people named in Achaemenid Persian inscriptions of the late 6th century BCE, probably living in Fergana and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamir-mountains">Pamirs</a>. Their name is usually taken to mean 'hauma-drinking' or 'hauma-preparing' Saka, after the ritual drink of Iranian religion. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> calls them the Amyrgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> and says they served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a>' army against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p></div>
